  "description": "MicroCLR is a SimCLR-based contrastive self-supervised learning framework for gut microbiome disease classification. It implements eight data augmentation strategies for CLR-transformed metagenomic profiles and benchmarks learned representations on four diseases (colorectal cancer, type 2 diabetes, inflammatory bowel disease, Parkinson's disease) across 1,286 samples from seven cohorts. Two novel augmentations are introduced: EcologicalAug (Spearman co-occurrence network-guided perturbation) and CohortStyleAug (inter-cohort mean-shift style transfer).",
